# Pages Layer - Streamlit UI Components

Streamlit pages layer that provides user-facing interfaces for Ethereum data analysis tools.

## Navigation Architecture
- Uses modern Streamlit `st.navigation` API with structured sections
- Home page serves as dashboard entry point with resource links
- Analysis pages organized under `analysis/` subdirectory with modular structure

## Page Structure Pattern
Each analysis component follows consistent modular architecture:
- `page.py` - Main Streamlit interface and user interaction logic
- Leverages shared utilities from `../shared/` for data operations and UI components
- Maintains separation between presentation layer and business logic

## Key Constraints
- Pages must be self-contained but leverage shared utilities for consistency
- Use absolute imports with proper path management for analysis subdirectories
- Follow Streamlit session state management with prefixed keys for conflict prevention